    accTitle: Frontend — what the reader sees and does
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. The workspace has a schema explorer and a question-and-answer area. Users browse table names, ask questions, watch progress, optionally cancel, then inspect the SQL, answer, or error. A successful table can be explored and downloaded without rerunning the query.
    %% Companion guide: docs/frontend.md

    WORKSPACE["Your workspace"]:::view
    SCHEMA["Schema explorer: Browse tables and columns"]:::view
    FILTER["Search or refresh the table list"]:::view
    QUESTION["Question area: Ask or follow up"]:::view
    WAIT["While the app works: Watch progress or cancel"]:::view
    RESPONSE["Response area: SQL preview, answer, or clear error"]:::view
    TABLE["Result table: Sort, page, and resize columns"]:::view
    EXPORT["Download CSV: Export the loaded rows"]:::data

    WORKSPACE -->|1.a. Ask a question| QUESTION
    QUESTION -->|2.a| WAIT
    WAIT -->|3| RESPONSE
    RESPONSE -->|4. Rows returned| TABLE
    TABLE -->|5| EXPORT
    WORKSPACE -->|1.b. Optional browsing| SCHEMA
    SCHEMA -->|2.b| FILTER

